    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6aDf2H",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3802801939,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.Microservices/VAA.EAPI.Microservices.Retail.Holidays/Triggers/Http/BookingController.cs",
      "line": 172,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1742#discussion_r3802801939",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "`RetrieveDocumentService.RetrieveDocument` throws `ArgumentException`/`InvalidOperationException` for expected validation/policy failures (disallowed host, non-PDF, oversize, redirects/unavailable, DNS restrictions). Since the controller doesn’t catch these, they will likely surface as 500s rather than controlled EAPI errors. Consider catching expected exceptions here (or refactoring the service to return a Result/Status) and map them to `Status.BadRequest` / `Status.NotFound` / a controlled technical error status, consistent with the existing `ResultExtention` pattern.",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Fixed in BookingController.RetrieveDocument: ArgumentException now returns the established BadRequest response and InvalidOperationException returns a controlled technical-error response, so expected service validation/policy failures no longer escape the endpoint. Added OpenAPI 400/500 responses and controller coverage for both mappings. Verification: Retail Holidays tests passed (97/97); the Microsoft Testing Platform ignored the requested VSTest filter/logger/coverage settings, so it emitted no TRX and the repository analyser could not run."
    }
  ],
